35,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Oh boy, I found some tricky stuff! The whole-building lets have non-refundable deposits, meaning if someone cancels late, the rest of us have to cover their cost. That's a bit scary!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shizue,,It's a bit sad to see that some of our dear members didn't join us last time. I've learned that the magic of mixing different year-groups really happens during those quiet evenings together in one place.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The cooking duty last year was a significant burden, taking two hours a day from the organizers. Also, transport costs fluctuate wildly depending on the distance, becoming the largest expense for far-off trips.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Rin,,The inland centers sound like a nightmare! Eight people to a room and a strict bedtime? We'll be exhausted! And our own hall is way too crowded to be any good.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"The public booking process is quite tedious, requiring a nine-page application and a lottery. Also, about a third of our members can't make it by nine in the morning without staying overnight.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Ryuji, if transport costs are that high for far-off trips, maybe we should stay closer? I'm still worried about those non-refundable deposits for whole buildings, though!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Misaki, it's a shame so many struggle with the early trains. Perhaps a place where we can all settle in together for the night would make it easier for everyone to join us.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Mio, staying local would certainly stabilize the budget. More importantly, we should prioritize a location with catering. If we have to cook for everyone, the organizers will lose too much training time.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Ryuji, I agree! If we're already tired from bad sleep, cooking for everyone will just make it worse. We need a place where we can actually relax and recharge!","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Shizue, staying overnight would solve the train issue, but we have to be careful. If we choose a public center, the lottery and paperwork are a huge risk if our dates change.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Misaki, a lottery sounds so stressful! I'd hate for us to plan everything and then not get the spot. But if we go with a private inn, we have to be super careful about who commits to coming!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Mio, you're right to be careful, but I worry more about the hearts of our members. If we don't create a space where they feel they belong, they might not come at all.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shizue, while the atmosphere is important, we must be practical about the labor involved. If the organizers are exhausted from cooking and logistics, they won't be able to foster that sense of belonging.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Ryuji, exactly! We can't be ""heartfelt"" if we're grumpy because we're tired. If we're squeezed eight to a room like those other clubs, we'll all be too cranky to have any fun!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Ryuji, I agree that practicality is key. If we want to avoid both the cooking burden and the lottery risks, we need a destination that is easy to book and provides meals, without being too far to drive.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Mio,,"I'm totally with you, Misaki! A place that's easy to book and has meals sounds like a dream. I just hope we can find a way to handle the costs so no one gets stuck paying extra!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"It sounds like we are all looking for a place of peace and ease. If we find a cozy spot that takes care of the meals, we can spend our energy on getting to know one another instead.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,I agree. A location that provides catering and is relatively close by will minimize both the financial risk and the physical toll on the organizers. We should avoid any option that requires self-catering.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Rin,,I'm with you all! Let's just make sure it's not a place where we're all crammed together like sardines. We need real beds and some peace and quiet so we can actually wake up feeling energized!,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"It seems we are in agreement on the priorities. We need a location that is accessible, provides catering to save us from cooking, and has a straightforward booking process to avoid the lottery.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Misaki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
57,3,,status,Rin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
58,3,,status,Mio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
59,3,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Campus Intensive sounds a bit boring, and the Coastal Lodge is way too far! Plus, that whole-building let at the lodge sounds like a financial risk if people cancel. I'm leaning toward B!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"The Mountain Training Centre sounds a bit crowded, and I worry that shared dormitories might not encourage the kind of warm, personal connection we need. I'm wondering if the Coastal Lodge might be more cozy.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Option B is a risk because it uses the municipal system, which Misaki mentioned involves a tedious lottery and paperwork. Option C is too far, which would spike transport costs and increase the logistical burden.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Rin,,"Option B is a total no-go! I already saw that inland centers cram eight people to a room with strict bedtimes. We'll be exhausted! Option A is too crowded, so I'm voting for the Coastal Lodge!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"Option B is out because of the lottery and paperwork risks. Option C is too far, which increases transport costs and financial uncertainty. Option A is the most stable and predictable choice.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Misaki, Option A is stable, but isn't it a bit dull? Still, if the Coastal Lodge is too far and Option B is a lottery nightmare, maybe A is the safest for our wallets!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Mio, safety is important, but I worry that staying on campus might keep everyone in their usual circles. A change of scenery, like the lodge, often helps people open up to one another.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shizue, a change of scenery is a luxury we cannot afford if it means the organizers spend the entire camp on duty. Option C's distance and the potential for self-catering risks are too high.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Ryuji, but the lodge says meals are arranged through the owner! That means no cooking for us! And it's way better than being sardines in a dorm or stuck at school. Let's go for the adventure!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Rin, adventure is fine, but ""arranged through the owner"" can be vague. Without a fixed rate sheet, we risk another budget shortfall. Option A allows us to control costs precisely and avoids the risk of non-refundable deposits.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Mio,,"@Misaki, you're making a lot of sense! I really don't want to deal with the stress of someone canceling and the rest of us paying for it. Option A is definitely the most fair for everyone's budget!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Mio, I understand your worry, but if we stay on campus, I fear we will lose the chance to truly bond. A cozy lodge where we all stay together could be the key to bringing our year-groups closer.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shizue, bonding is a secondary goal to the actual training. If we choose Option C, the distance and the logistics of a new venue will likely fall on the organizers, repeating last year's mistake. Option A is the only rational choice.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Rin,,"@Ryuji, you're being too grumpy! The lodge has an owner for meals, so you won't be stuck in the kitchen. Option A is just school! We need a real trip where we can actually sleep and have fun!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Rin, school is where we have the most control. Option C is two prefectures away; the transport costs alone would be a gamble. I cannot support a plan with so many financial variables.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Mio,,"I'm torn because I love the idea of a trip, but Misaki and Ryuji are right about the risks. I can't shake that fear of non-refundable deposits! I'll vote for A to keep it fair.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Shizue,,"It is a difficult choice, but my heart tells me that the bond between our members is the most precious thing. I will vote for the Coastal Lodge to bring us all together.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,"Option A is the only choice that guarantees the organizers can actually train. Option B is a bureaucratic gamble, and Option C is a logistical and financial burden. I am voting for A.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Rin,,I'm not voting for A or B! A is just school and B is a sleep-deprivation trap. The lodge is the only place we can actually relax and wake up happy. I'm voting for C!,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Misaki,,"I agree with Ryuji. Option B is too risky and Option C is financially unpredictable. To ensure we don't face another budget gap, we must choose the most stable path. I'm voting for A.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
